WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.366
This is recorded Azure output at original
event

00:00:03.366 --> 00:00:06.732
timing. The walkthrough follows streaming
decisions and message

00:00:06.732 --> 00:00:10.099
triage; it does not make live model
requests.

00:00:10.499 --> 00:00:15.280
Stream consumes a conversation
incrementally. Token events update the

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:20.061
transcript; separate model decision events
update the probability charts.

00:00:20.461 --> 00:00:23.765
Pause freezes the playback timeline. The
question

00:00:23.765 --> 00:00:27.070
schema combines Boolean probabilities, a
categorical topic,

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:29.902
and an ordinal customer mood score.

00:00:30.302 --> 00:00:33.244
Each model allows one in flight request

00:00:33.244 --> 00:00:36.186
and then evaluates the latest available
snapshot.

00:00:36.186 --> 00:00:39.128
Intermediate snapshots can be skipped, so
these

00:00:39.128 --> 00:00:42.070
call counts do not represent identical
sampling.

00:00:43.247 --> 00:00:46.264
Triage feeds the same forty messages into
both

00:00:46.264 --> 00:00:49.281
lanes. The worker limits are eight for
Decision

00:00:49.281 --> 00:00:52.298
One and four for the language model
baseline.

00:00:52.698 --> 00:00:56.065
This burst arrives at twenty messages per
second.

00:00:56.065 --> 00:00:59.432
The counters and result events show how
outstanding

00:00:59.432 --> 00:01:01.958
work accumulates under those worker
limits.

00:01:02.358 --> 00:01:05.471
The in queue counter includes requests
still running.

00:01:05.471 --> 00:01:08.585
Average wait is arrival to completion
time, so

00:01:08.585 --> 00:01:11.699
it includes both queuing and model request
time.

00:01:12.099 --> 00:01:16.097
Playback resumes from the same event
position. Worker counts

00:01:16.097 --> 00:01:20.095
and request latencies both influence the
outcome; this is

00:01:20.095 --> 00:01:24.092
a pipeline demonstration, not a controlled
concurrency benchmark. Throughput

00:01:24.092 --> 00:01:28.090
uses the original recording clock, not the
playback speed.

00:01:29.816 --> 00:01:33.460
Each completed message retains its
classification and

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:37.105
extracted spans. The dashboard aggregates
those decisions

00:01:37.105 --> 00:01:40.749
into department, severity, and churn risk
counts.

00:01:41.149 --> 00:01:45.712
Replay files preserve inputs, question
schemas, model outputs, and

00:01:45.712 --> 00:01:50.274
original timing. New inputs require live
mode, using WebSocket

00:01:50.274 --> 00:01:54.329
events and Entra ID authentication on the
backend.
